CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ matching: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ mismatching: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A partial specialization of a variable template whose argument list ends in
a pack expansion, constructible_v0<true, tup<Dests...>, Srcs...>, matched
only when the number of arguments equalled the written ones.  The MSVC
STL's _Tuple_constructible_v0 has this shape, and std::tuple<int, int> t(1,
2) found no constructor.
